{"documents":[{"title":"Grobid CLI","url":"/","body":"Convert PDF articles to Markdown so AI can work better with them. Built upon GROBID . The Problem AI models struggle to extract clean, structured content from PDFs. Raw PDFs are messy — headers, footers, citations, tables, and figures make it hard for LLMs to parse and reason about academic papers or documents. The Solution grobid cli uses GROBID (GeneRation Of BIbliographic Data) to extract structured content from PDFs and convert them to clean Markdown with rich metadata in frontmatter. This makes documents AI-friendly and easy to process. Features PDF → TEI → Markdown : Full conversion pipeline using GROBID's TEI XML extraction Auto-starts GROBID : Automatically launches a GROBID Docker container if not already running Rich metadata : Extracts title, authors, journal, year, volume, issue, pages, DOI and adds them as YAML frontmatter Structured output : Preserves abstract, article sections, references, tables, lists, and formulas Simple CLI : One command to convert all PDFs in pdf/ directory Resumable : Skips already converted TEI/XML and Markdown files Quick Start Prerequisites Docker (for auto-starting GROBID) Python 3.10+ Installation pip install -e . # or uv pip install -e . Usage Put your PDFs in a pdf/ directory Run the converter Get TEI XML in tei/ and Markdown in md/ grobid Or set a custom data directory: GROBID_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data grobid Output Example --- title: \u0026quot;Paper Title\u0026quot; authors: \u0026quot;Author One, Author Two\u0026quot; year: 2024 journal: \u0026quot;Journal Name\u0026quot; volume: \u0026quot;10\u0026quot; doi: \u0026quot;10.1234/example\u0026quot; doi_link: \u0026quot;https://doi.org/10.1234/example\u0026quot; --- # Paper Title **Authors:** Author One, Author Two ## Abstract ... ## Article ... ## References ... Directory Structure your-project/ ├── pdf/ # Input PDFs ├── tei/ # Generated TEI XML (intermediate) └── md/ # Output Markdown files Environment Variables Variable Default Description GROBID_DATA_DIR / ARTICLES_DATA_DIR Current directory Data directory containing pdf/ , tei/ , md/ GROBID_PORT 8070 Port for GROBID server GROBID_IMAGE grobid/grobid:0.9.1-crf Docker image for GROBID GROBID_CONTAINER grobid-cli Docker container name Development make lint # Run linters make format # Format code make test # Run tests make build # Build binary with PyInstaller Why Grobid CLI? The problem: AI does not work well with PDFs. Raw PDF text extraction loses structure, citations break context, and formatting confuses models. The solution: grobid cli leverages GROBID's state-of-the-art PDF parsing to produce clean, structured Markdown that LLMs can understand and reason about effectively. License MIT License"}],"trigramIndex":{"\u0026qu":[0],"(fo":[0],"(ge":[0],"(in":[0],"**a":[0],"*au":[0],"---":[0],"-ar":[0],"-cl":[0],"-cr":[0],"-fr":[0],"-of":[0],"-pr":[0],"-st":[0],"-th":[0],"...":[0],".1-":[0],".10":[0],".12":[0],".9.":[0],".or":[0],"//d":[0],"/10":[0],"/da":[0],"/do":[0],"/ex":[0],"/gr":[0],"/pa":[0],"/to":[0],"/xm":[0],"0\u0026q":[0],"0.1":[0],"0.9":[0],"024":[0],"070":[0],"1-c":[0],"10\u0026":[0],"10+":[0],"10.":[0],"123":[0],"202":[0],"234":[0],"3.1":[0],"34/":[0],"4/e":[0],"807":[0],"9.1":[0],":**":[0],"://":[0],":0.":[0],";10":[0],";au":[0],";ht":[0],";jo":[0],";pa":[0],"=/p":[0],"_co":[0],"_da":[0],"_di":[0],"_im":[0],"_li":[0],"_po":[0],"a_d":[0],"abl":[0],"abo":[0],"abs":[0],"aca":[0],"act":[0],"ada":[0],"add":[0],"ade":[0],"ady":[0],"age":[0],"ai-":[0],"ain":[0],"ake":[0],"al,":[0],"al:":[0],"all":[0],"alr":[0],"ame":[0],"aml":[0],"amp":[0],"an,":[0],"and":[0],"ape":[0],"aph":[0],"ar,":[0],"ar:":[0],"ard":[0],"are":[0],"ari":[0],"ark":[0],"ars":[0],"art":[0],"ary":[0],"aso":[0],"asy":[0],"ata":[0],"ate":[0],"ath":[0],"ati":[0],"att":[0],"atu":[0],"aul":[0],"aun":[0],"aut":[0],"bet":[0],"bib":[0],"bid":[0],"bin":[0],"ble":[0],"bli":[0],"bou":[0],"bre":[0],"bst":[0],"bui":[0],"cad":[0],"cal":[0],"can":[0],"cen":[0],"ces":[0],"